# Red Lentil Caldo with Mexican Spices

Adapted from lentils.md research document

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] Optional: 1 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } for sauteing
- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, diced
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 cup [red lentils]{ ing="red-lentils" }, rinsed
- [ ] 2 medium [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, chopped
- [ ] 2 medium [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, diced (or 1 can diced tomatoes, 14 oz)
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground coriander]{ ing="ground-coriander" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [turmeric]{ ing="turmeric" } (optional)
- [ ] Optional: 1 [dried guajillo chile]{ ing="dried-guajillo-chile" }, seeded
- [ ] 4 cups [vegetable broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" } or water
- [ ] [Salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" } to taste

### For Serving

- [ ] [Lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }
- [ ] [Olive oil drizzle]{ ing="olive-oil-drizzle" }
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
- [ ] [Crusty bread]{ ing="crusty-bread" } or tortillas

## Recipe

1. (Optional) Saute [onion]{ ing="onion" } and [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } in [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } in Instant Pot on saute mode for 2-3 minutes
1. Add [red lentils]{ ing="red-lentils" }, [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, spices, [guajillo chile]{ ing="dried-guajillo-chile" } (if using), and [broth]{ ing="vegetable-broth" }
1. Cook on high pressure for 8 minutes
1. Quick release pressure
1. Optional: Blend partially or fully for creamy texture (remove [chile]{ ing="dried-guajillo-chile" } first)
1. Season with [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" } to taste
1. Serve with [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }, [olive oil drizzle]{ ing="olive-oil-drizzle" }, and [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }

## Notes

- Red lentils cook quickly and break down naturally, creating a creamy texture without dairy; their nutty flavor complements the Mexican spices
- Very digestible for kids and toddlers
- Excellent iron and vitamin A combination from lentils and carrots
- For thicker soup, use less broth or simmer on saute mode after cooking
- For thinner soup, add more broth after pressure cooking
- Guajillo chile adds mild heat and depth; omit for completely mild version
